.TH MUEMACS 1 "2025" "μEmacs 0.0.23" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
muEmacs \- small, fast Linux terminal text editor (μEmacs)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B muEmacs
\fR[\fB+\fR\fIn\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-g\fR\fIn\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-s\fR\fIpattern\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-r\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-n\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-v\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-e\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB--help\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB--version\fR]
\fR[\fIFILE\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBμEmacs\fR is a modernization of Linus Torvalds' tiny uEmacs editor for contemporary Linux terminals.
It retains the original philosophy: small codebase, instant startup, sane defaults, and classic Emacs-style
key bindings in a pure TUI. This implementation focuses on Linux, UTF\-8 correctness, terminal fidelity,
and robust behavior without bloat.
.PP
Notable traits:
.IP \(bu 2
Drop\-in build and install: compile fast; run everywhere Linux has \fIncursesw\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
UTF\-8 by default with correct display width and bracketed paste handling.
.IP \(bu 2
Single binary at runtime; predictable paths for data files.
.SH OPTIONS
The following options are recognized on the command line (a subset mirrors classic uEmacs behavior):
.TP
.B --help
Show a brief usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.BI + n
Start at line \fIn\fR of the first file. If \fIn\fR is omitted (plain \fB+\fR), start at end of file.
.TP
.BI -g n
Go to line \fIn\fR after startup (equivalent to \fB+\fR\fIn\fR).
.TP
.BI -s pattern
Search forward for \fIpattern\fR on startup (non\-interactive initial search).
.TP
.B -v
View\-only mode (read\-only buffers).
.TP
.B -e
Explicitly enable editing (cancels a prior \fB-v\fR in argument order).
.TP
.B -r
Restricted mode: disallow file writes, shell escapes, and similar operations.
.TP
.B -n
Accept NUL (\e0) characters in input files.
.TP
.BI @ file
Execute startup macro file \fIfile\fR before entering the editor (classic uEmacs feature).
.SH KEY BINDINGS (ABRIDGED)
μEmacs uses Emacs\-style bindings. Selected defaults:
.TP
.B C\-x C\-c
Exit μEmacs.
.TP
.B C\-x C\-s
Save current buffer.
.TP
.B C\-x C\-f
Find/open file.
.TP
.B C\-g
Cancel current operation.
.TP
.B ESC (Meta prefix)
Use ESC as Meta, e.g., \fBM\-x\fR to execute a named command.
.TP
.B C\-s, C\-r
Incremental search forward, reverse.
.TP
.B C\-Space, C\-w, M\-w, C\-y
Set mark; kill region; copy region; yank.
.PP
For a full list of commands, see the project README and in\-editor help (describe\-bindings, describe\-key).
