.SS Numeric Arguments and M\-x
Use \fBC\-u\fR (universal argument) to prefix counts; ESC may be used as Meta for M\-x and other Meta bindings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/muemacs/editor/settings.json
System defaults for editor behavior (installed with the program).
.TP
.I /usr/share/muemacs/keymaps
Default keymap overlays.
.TP
.I /usr/share/muemacs/terminal
Terminal integration snippets (e.g., kitty config).
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/muEmacs.desktop
Desktop entry to launch μEmacs in a terminal emulator.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Specifies terminal type; use a modern entry such as \fBxterm\-256color\fR or a terminal\-specific entry.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
If set to \fBtruecolor\fR, enables 24\-bit color sequences in capable terminals.
.TP
.B LANG, LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE
Should be set to a UTF\-8 locale for correct processing and display of Unicode text.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns \fB0\fR on success, non\-zero on error.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are reported in the echo area (status line) and via a non\-zero exit status when applicable.
Restricted mode (\fB-r\fR) prevents operations such as file writes and shell escapes.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Two command names are available after install: \fBμEmacs\fR (Unicode) and the ASCII\-friendly alias \fBmuEmacs\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
This build targets Linux only and links against \fIncursesw\fR; it is TUI\-only by design.
.IP \(bu 2
Defaults ship with the program and are intentionally simple; see \fIFILES\fR.
.SH HISTORY
μEmacs descends from MicroEMACS (1985) through Petri Kutvonen’s uEmacs/PK to Linus Torvalds’ tiny uEmacs.
This build preserves that lineage (small, portable, fast) while modernizing terminal and UTF\-8 behavior.
