.SH COMMANDS (NAMED)
All editor functions are available via \fBM\-x\fR followed by the command name.
This section lists commonly used commands, grouped by category.
.SS Core
.TP
.B abort-command
Cancel current operation.
.TP
.B exit-emacs, quick-exit
Exit editor; quick variant saves and exits.
.TP
.B help, execute-named-command
Display help; prompt for command by name (M\-x).
.SS Buffers & Files
.TP
.B find-file, view-file, read-file, write-file, save-file, insert-file
Open, view, insert, save, and write buffers/files.
.TP
.B list-buffers, select-buffer, next-buffer, delete-buffer, name-buffer
Manage buffers and buffer list.
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B beginning-of-file, end-of-file, beginning-of-line, end-of-line, goto-line
Move to file/line boundaries and arbitrary line numbers.
.TP
.B next-line, previous-line, forward-character, backward-character, next-word, previous-word
Basic motion commands.
.SS Editing & Regions
.TP
.B delete-next-character, delete-previous-character, delete-next-word, delete-previous-word
Delete characters and words.
.TP
.B kill-to-end-of-line, kill-region, copy-region, yank, yank-pop, yank-clipboard
Kill/copy/paste operations and clipboard integration.
.TP
.B quote-character, transpose-characters, duplicate-line, move-line-up, move-line-down
Editing helpers and line manipulation.
.SS Text Formatting
.TP
.B case-word-upper, case-word-lower, case-word-capitalize
Change case for words.
.TP
.B case-region-upper, case-region-lower
Change case for region.
.TP
.B fill-paragraph, justify-paragraph, count-words
Paragraph formatting and statistics.
.SS Search & Replace
.TP
.B search-forward, search-reverse, incremental-search, reverse-incremental-search
Forward/reverse search modes.
.TP
.B replace-string, query-replace-string, hunt-forward, hunt-backward
Replacement and repeated search.
.SS Windows & Display
.TP
.B split-current-window, delete-window, delete-other-windows, next-window, previous-window
Window management.
.TP
.B grow-window, shrink-window, resize-window
Resize windows.
.TP
.B clear-and-redraw, redraw-display, update-screen
Screen refresh and redraw.
.SS Macros & Scripting
.TP
.B begin-macro, end-macro, execute-macro, store-macro
Record, run, and store macros.
.TP
.B execute-buffer, execute-file, execute-command-line, execute-program, shell-command, pipe-command, filter-buffer
Execute buffers/files/commands, run external programs, and filter regions through commands.
.SS Configuration & Modes
.TP
.B bind-to-key, unbind-key, describe-key, describe-bindings
Key binding management and help.
.TP
.B add-mode, delete-mode, add-global-mode, delete-global-mode
Toggle buffer and global modes.
.TP
.B set, set-column-width, writing-mode, exit-writing-mode
Set variables; writing helpers and wrap configuration.
.TP
.B set-mark, exchange-point-and-mark, unmark-buffer
Mark management and region selection.
.SH MODES
Buffer and global modes alter editing behavior. Toggle with \fBadd-mode\fR / \fBdelete-mode\fR (buffer) and
\fBadd-global-mode\fR / \fBdelete-global-mode\fR (global). Common modes:
.TP
.B WRAP
Enable word wrap at the fill column.
.TP
.B CMODE
C language editing conveniences.
.TP
.B SPELL
Spell-related hooks (if available).
.TP
.B EXACT
Exact (case-sensitive) searches by default.
.TP
.B VIEW
View-only (read-only) buffer behavior.
.TP
.B OVER
Overwrite mode (typing replaces characters).
.TP
.B MAGIC
Enable regex-lite (NFA) “MAGIC” search engine.
.TP
.B ASAVE
Auto-save after a configured threshold.
.TP
.B UTF-8
Force UTF-8 operations and display handling.
.SH VARIABLES
Variables control editor behavior and modeline display. Set with \fBset\fR (e.g., \fBset ruler 1\fR). Useful variables:
.TP
.B fillcol
Target column for wrap/fill operations (default 72).
.TP
.B highlightline \(em hilinestyle
Enable current-line highlight; choose style (0 none, 1 underline, 2 bold, 3 dim).
.TP
.B ruler \(em rulerstyle \(em rulercol
Enable a vertical column ruler; style as above; set the target column (default 80).
.TP
.B modeline_show_git / _stats / _modes / _position
Toggle git branch indicator, stats, modes, and cursor position in the modeline.
.TP
.B column_width
Preferred wrap column for writing; used by \fBwriting-mode\fR and \fBset-column-width\fR.
.TP
.B scrollcount
Number of lines to scroll for paging commands.
.TP
.B overlap
Line overlap when paging.
.TP
.B nullflag
Accept NUL (\e0) characters in files.
.TP
.B restflag
Restricted mode (disables writes and external commands).
